# BuildKit honours `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile, so this
# lives in the platform repo (not the build-context root). Patterns are relative
# to the build context (the parent dir holding dpp-engine/).
# Keep the context to Rust source only.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.github
**/dist
**/.astro
dpp-web
docs
public
research
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
# Local [patch.crates-io] override — never bake the sibling-path patch into an
# image that must build from crates.io.
**/.cargo/config.toml
# The toolchain file stays out of the context. Inside it, rustup honoured the
# channel it names over the base image and fetched that compiler mid-build —
# a compiler neither the FROM tag nor the provenance attestation records. The
# FROM tag is pinned to the same version instead, and CI's images job fails
# when the two differ.
**/rust-toolchain.toml
